=================================
SDLHana Installation & Build Guide
=================================

SDLHana uses modern CMake (version 3.25 or higher) for cross-platform building on Windows, macOS, and Linux. All core dependencies (SDL3, SDL3_mixer, SDL3_ttf) are automatically resolved and compiled via CMake FetchContent.

Prerequisites
-------------
- A modern C++23 compliant compiler:
  - Windows: Visual Studio 2022 / 2026 (MSVC) or MinGW GCC
  - macOS: Xcode / Clang
  - Linux: GCC 13+ or Clang 16+
- CMake 3.25 or higher

Building from Source
--------------------

1. Configure the CMake build directory:
   cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release

2. Build the project:
   cmake --build build --config Release

3. Run the executable:
   - Windows: .\build\Release\sdlhana.exe (or .\build\Debug\sdlhana.exe)
   - Linux / macOS: ./build/Release/sdlhana

Custom Build Generators & Options
---------------------------------

- Ninja Generator:
  cmake -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build

- Visual Studio Solution (Windows):
  cmake -B build -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" (or "Visual Studio 18 2026")
  cmake --build build --config Release
